### Purpose of &quot;%matplotlib inline&quot;

The `%matplotlib inline` command is used in Python to display plots and charts directly in the Jupyter Notebook or other interactive environments. When enabled, it automatically embeds the matplotlib plot in the notebook, allowing you to visualize data in real-time as you work. This feature is particularly useful for data analysis, visualization, and prototyping, as it enables seamless interaction with the code and allows for easy exploration of complex data sets.

