<p>I'm getting an error when trying to start my program:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>An attempt was made to access a socket in a way forbidden by its access permissions.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't understand why... it worked fine, and now it doesn't.</p>
<p>I am streaming with VLC, and I want to receive the packets, do some reports, and then restream local to a player.</p>

Answers:
import socket

def close_socket(sock):
    sock.close()

def shutdown_socket(sock, mode):
    if mode == 'shutdown':
        sock.setsockopt(socket.SOL_SOCKET, socket.SO_SHUTDOWN, 1)
        sock.settimeout(0)
    else:
        raise ValueError("Invalid shutdown mode")

# Example usage:
sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
shutdown_socket(sock, 'shutdown')
close_socket(sock)

