Title: How can I access and process nested objects, arrays, or JSON?.
Body: <p>I have a nested data structure containing objects and arrays. How can I extract the information, i.e. access a specific or multiple values (or keys)?</p>

<p>For example:</p>

<pre><code>var data = {
    code: 42,
    items: [{
        id: 1,
        name: 'foo'
    }, {
        id: 2,
        name: 'bar'
    }]
};
</code></pre>

<p>How could I access the <code>name</code> of the second item in <code>items</code>?</p>

Answers:
def get_item_name(data, item_index):
    # Get the index of the item in the 'items' array
    item_index = item_index % len(data.items)
    # Return the name of the item at the current index
    return data.items[item_index].name

var data = {
    code: 42,
    items: [{
        id: 1,
        name: 'foo'
    }, {
        id: 2,
        name: 'bar'
    }]
};

console.log(get_item_name(data, 1));  // Outputs: bar

