Title: Sorting object property by values.
Body: <p>If I have a JavaScript object such as:</p>

<pre><code>var list = {
  "you": 100, 
  "me": 75, 
  "foo": 116, 
  "bar": 15
};
</code></pre>

<p>Is there a way to sort the properties based on value? So that I end up with</p>

<pre><code>list = {
  "bar": 15, 
  "me": 75, 
  "you": 100, 
  "foo": 116
};
</code></pre>

Answers:
def sort_object_by_value(dictionary):
    return dict(sorted(dictionary.items(), key=lambda item: item[1]))

list = {
  "you": 100, 
  "me": 75, 
  "foo": 116, 
  "bar": 15
}

print(sort_object_by_value(list))  # Output: {'bar': 15, 'you': 100, 'foo': 116}

